    "answer": {
      "short": "23 nuggets.\n\nThe totals 24–28 are possible; adding boxes of 5 gives every larger total.",
      "worked": "For 23 nuggets, the possible numbers of boxes of 7 are 0, 1, 2 and 3. The remaining totals are 23, 16, 9 and 2; none is divisible by 5. Thus 23 nuggets cannot be purchased.\n\nFive consecutive larger totals can be purchased:\n$$\\begin{align*}24&=2\\times5+2\\times7\\\\25&=5\\times5\\\\26&=1\\times5+3\\times7\\\\27&=4\\times5+1\\times7\\\\28&=4\\times7\\end{align*}$$\nEvery total greater than 28 is one of these totals plus a positive multiple of 5, so it can be purchased by adding boxes of 5. Therefore, the largest impossible total is 23 nuggets.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 100
